<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mali Federation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1959">1959</a>–<a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a> Federation was a union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> and the Sudanese Republic, the former French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, formed in 1959 within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-community">French Community</a>. It became independent on 20 June 1960 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakar-senegal">Dakar</a> as capital, but disputes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-sedar-senghor">Léopold Sédar Senghor</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modibo-keita">Modibo Keïta</a> led Senegal to withdraw in August 1960. The Sudanese Republic then proclaimed itself the Republic of Mali.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mali-federation.jpg" alt="Mali Federation" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mali_(1959%E2%80%931961).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
